  "oracle": "Same existing D3D9 implementation compiled into a private static archive,consumed by a real loader DLL. Build artifact assertions verify namespace,stdcall ABI,no CRT/system D3D9 dependency and separate trace path. Relational reference requires global uniqueness for all six device/declaration handles,the same session tuple across three module Hellos,and a single final SessionEnd after explicit destruction. SDK factory QI/GetDirect3D identities and exact final refs prove real COM objects. Expected pixels are independent constant colors,not derived from captured data.",
  "scope": "Stage4K1 prepares a linkable D3D9 core with prefixed factory/module lifecycle API and retail/diagnostic21-member archives including shared runtime. Minimal consumer exposes exactly one factory export. Ordinary DLL public exports remain intact,private diagnostics use distinct d3d9_core_trace filenames,and D3D8 headers can include forward-declared boundary without mixing SDK types. XP loads/unloads private consumer twice while ordinary D3D9 device stays alive,using three factories/devices,three cache declarations,three Hellos in one owner/session and five UP/readbacks;only one final session/owner end. Dual GPU validates320 pixels and empty maps before SessionEnd and genuine owner release. Initial freestanding flags caused CRT symbol references in SDK memory operations;static core now uses the already accepted frontend compilation configuration. Actual D3D8 device/resource wrapping,PP/caps/state conversions,full identity mapping,HAL/games/FPS and stages4/5/6 remain open. D3D8/DDraw and host/protocol/shader/bundle unchanged.",
